# SKY-BACKDROP: the Starter procedural sky follows the atmosphere sun (UE: SkyAtmosphere is the one sky source).
# Proven 10-27: the ProceduralSky pass IS the visible sky (forced output reaches the frame), but its packed
# block's sun direction stays at the load-time sun when SunElevation changes (probe: v[0].y > 0.5 at 45 AND 10).
Дано run Scene "Open Scene Starter.desce"
Дано run Entity "Sun"
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.FOV 60
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,300,0
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.811,0.4,0.579
Когда --subject selection set SunElevation 45
Тогда-вид 1_noon blue sky, the sun disc visible
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.811,0.0,0.579
Когда --subject selection set SunElevation 3
Тогда-вид 2_sunset orange sunset at the horizon, the disc at the horizon
# 3_colors: ZenithColor is not settable through `selection set` (only Transform offers properties);
# needs a Starter copy with ZenithColor 1,0,0 opened by "Open Scene", or a Details-path setter.
